{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויגדו לו", :translit "vayagdu lo", :gloss "and they told him"} {:he "חסר יו\"ד", :translit "chaser yud", :gloss "deficient [in the letter] yud"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of ויגדו (missing yod) signals that the brothers delayed reporting to Jacob until they first dissolved a ban of silence imposed by ten men."}], :frame {:text "The brothers had imposed a ban of silence (cherem) upon themselves so that none would reveal to Jacob that Joseph was alive; this ban required a court of ten to annul. The word ויגדו appears with a missing yod, signaling the delay in telling Jacob until the ban was formally released.", :sources ["Genesis 45:26"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of ויגדו (missing yod) signals that the brothers delayed reporting to Jacob until they first dissolved a ban of silence imposed by ten men.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:11:41.620459519Z", :model "glm-5.2"}